course: dictionary
lesson: 10910
title: Vitamins: a word with clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A vitamin is a tiny natural part of food that your body needs to stay healthy. You cannot see it, but it is there in fruit, vegetables and other foods. «Vitamins are needed in small amounts, and most must come from food because the body can't make enough of them.» Small amounts means you need only a little, but you need it regularly.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is meant. «Fruit and veg of different colours give different vitamins and minerals» is about food. But «a vitamin pill» is a pill with vitamins in it, and pills are medicine. Ask yourself: is this sentence about food, or about a pill?
explain: Each vitamin has a letter name, such as A, C or D, and each one has its own job. Vitamin C helps the body heal, vitamin A helps your eyes, and vitamin D helps keep your bones strong. The letter tells you which vitamin you are reading about.
fact: A vitamin is a tiny natural substance in food that your body needs to stay healthy.
fact: Each vitamin has a letter name, like vitamin A, B, C, D, E or K.
fact: «Vitamin D» comes from sunlight, and it helps keep your bones strong.
fact: «Too much vitamin A can be harmful», so vitamin pills are medicine and should only be taken with an adult.
fact: A balanced diet, with fruit and vegetables of many colours, gives you the vitamins you need.
exercise: «Vitamins are needed in small amounts, and most must come from food.» Where do most vitamins come from? | From the moon | *From food | From pills only | From the bottom of the sea
exercise: Which food is named as a good source of vitamin C? | Sugar cubes | Cheese | *Oranges | Bread
exercise: «Too much vitamin A can be harmful, so cod-liver oil should not be doubled up.» What does harmful mean? | Small and light | Very healthy | Tasty and sweet | *Bad for you, able to hurt you
test: «Reptiles need special UV lamps to make vitamin D for strong bones.» What is vitamin D needed for in this sentence? | *Strong bones | Clean teeth | Growing hair | Happy feelings
test: Ella says a vitamin pill is a sweet. Why is she wrong? | They are always taken without asking | *Vitamin pills are medicine and are only taken with an adult | They grow on trees | They are chocolate
exam: Jayden reads, «You never need to burn to make vitamin D.» What does this tell you? | Burning is good for your skin | You must burn in the sun to get vitamin D | *A short time outside in the sun is enough, so you do not need to burn | Vitamin D is found only in cod
